          <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Should I choose a rotary, foil, or T-blade trimmer for my back?</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
              Rotary blades tend to power through thick or curly hair well and hold an edge longer. Foil-style blades use rounded blade tips that are gentler on sensitive or bump-prone skin but may need more passes on very dense hair. T-blade heads are wider and faster for covering large flat areas but have a slightly steeper learning curve for blade angle. It depends on your hair texture, skin sensitivity, and how much surface area you need to cover.
